From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Raneri <kevin.raneri@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Nov 2021 00:37:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Pufferfish: Optimize mob spawning

Original license: GPL v3
Original project: https://github.com/pufferfish-gg/Pufferfish

This patch aims to reduce the main-thread impact of mob spawning by
offloading as much work as possible to other threads. It is possible for
inconsistencies to come up, but when they happen they never interfere
with the server's operation (they don't produce errors), and side
effects are limited to more or less mobs being spawned in any particular
tick.

It is possible to disable this optimization if it is not required or if
it interferes with any plugins. On servers with thousands of entities,
this can result in performance gains of up to 15%, which is significant
and, in my opinion, worth the low risk of minor mob-spawning-related
inconsistencies.

Imported into Kodama from Leaf (https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf) @ becd099200691927e35a419c9534835db7bf8b31, patch 0007-Pufferfish-Optimize-mob-spawning.patch.
Original license: GPL v3 (Pufferfish; stated in the patch header).
Kodama changes: Leaf's AsyncMobSpawning config module replaced by async.mob-spawning.enabled (restart required, read once at startup) via dev.kodama.async.AsyncSettings; offloading only applies with per-player mob spawns, and a failed count reports to the async-mob-spawning FeatureGuard and re-arms the next count.

diff --git a/src/main/java/dev/kodama/async/AsyncSettings.java b/src/main/java/dev/kodama/async/AsyncSettings.java
index 86c77ec22b176fd7aecc1ebcf690b8b2908ec11e..3ccd0ae94655335ecd230c307a3237d2c58d9a97 100644
--- a/src/main/java/dev/kodama/async/AsyncSettings.java
+++ b/src/main/java/dev/kodama/async/AsyncSettings.java
@@ -10,6 +10,9 @@ import org.checkerframework.checker.nullness.qual.Nullable;
 public final class AsyncSettings {
 
     public static final String PATHFINDING = "async-pathfinding";
+    public static final String MOB_SPAWNING = "async-mob-spawning";
+
+    private static volatile boolean mobSpawningEnabled; // read once by latchAsyncMobSpawning
 
     private static final ThreadLocal<Boolean> FORCE_SYNC_PATHFINDING = new ThreadLocal<>();
 
@@ -51,6 +54,23 @@ public final class AsyncSettings {
         void close();
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Reads the startup value of {@code async.mob-spawning.enabled}. Only the server startup calls this, right where it
+     * decides whether to start the mob spawning thread, so a reload can never enable offloading without that thread.
+     */
+    public static boolean latchAsyncMobSpawning() {
+        final KodamaGlobalConfiguration.Async section = section();
+        mobSpawningEnabled = section != null && section.mobSpawning.enabled.isTrue();
+        return mobSpawningEnabled;
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Whether mob counting is offloaded: the startup value, unless the {@link FeatureGuard} has switched it off.
+     */
+    public static boolean asyncMobSpawning() {
+        return mobSpawningEnabled && !FeatureGuard.isTripped(MOB_SPAWNING);
+    }
+
     /**
      * Read once when the pathfinding executor is created.
      */
